<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system repos.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system repos.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the U.S. banking system Wednesday morning via overnight system repurchase agreements, the Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>At 1010 EDT/1410 GMT, the overnight bank lending, or federal funds rate was trading at 5-7/16 percent, just below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>Analysts has expected an addition to reserves via overnight or term system RPs.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660 ))</p>
